id: pm-gh1478
title: "GH-1478: Read-output compaction splits valid emoji at 240 code units, crashing TOON and emitting lone surrogates in JSON"
description: "GitHub report https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1478. Bounded output compaction preserves valid Unicode prefixes in JSON and TOON through a shared primitive, without changing budget accounting or unbounded output."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,"area:sdk",github-intake
created_at: "2026-10-16T04:07:17.204Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T20:59:27.847Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-16T20:38:15.817Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-16T20:38:15.817Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Both ordinary and context-intent compaction preserve astral pairs across the cutoff and nested values; JSON and TOON render without manufactured lone surrogates; input immutability, unbounded reads, preserved exceptions and exact budget receipts remain covered"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: medium
confidence: medium
severity: high
resolution: "Use a shared Unicode-safe prefix in ordinary read-output budgets, context-intent compaction, recurrence receipts and compact diagnostic actions. Preserve intact surrogate pairs, exact budget accounting, input immutability, unbounded behavior and existing malformed-input rejection."
expected_result: "Valid astral characters at a truncation boundary never become lone surrogates or replacement characters in JSON or TOON, and every existing output ceiling remains enforced."
actual_result: "111 focused SDK, CLI, MCP, recurrence and diagnostic cases pass. Four prior-owner controls fail at intended assertions while three positive controls pass. Types, lint, global source quality, unchanged SDK surface and docs links pass. Hosted global coverage, final full review, reviewed merge and published-artifact verification remain required; Sentry status is not claimed resolved before that handoff."
